{"name":"Roseate Spoonbill","hex":"#e0adc4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"roseate spoonbill","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A species of spoonbill, Platalea ajaja."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roseate_spoonbill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roseate spoonbill","blocks":[{"text":"The roseate spoonbill is a social wading bird of the ibis and spoonbill family, Threskiornithidae. It is a resident breeder in both South and North America. The roseate spoonbill's pink color is diet-derived, consisting of the carotenoid pigment canthaxanthin, like the American flamingo."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Roseate_Spoonbill_-_Myakka_River_State_Park.jpg/330px-Roseate_Spoonbill_-_Myakka_River_State_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roseate_spoonbill","wikidata":"Q389664"},{"title":"Spoonbill","blocks":[{"text":"Spoonbills are a genus, Platalea, of large, long-legged wading birds. The spoonbills have a global distribution, being found on every continent except Antarctica. The genus name Platalea derives from Ancient Greek and means \"broad\", referring to the distinctive shape of the bill. Six species are recognised, which although usually placed in a single genus have sometimes been split into three genera."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Roseate_Spoonbill_-_Myakka_River_State_Park.jpg/330px-Roseate_Spoonbill_-_Myakka_River_State_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spoonbill","wikidata":"Q208488"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Roseate_spoonbill_%28Platalea_ajaja%29_young_adult_Rio_Napo.jpg/330px-Roseate_spoonbill_%28Platalea_ajaja%29_young_adult_Rio_Napo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wi